{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The present crisis in Puerto Rico is the culmination of decades of U.S. policies that distorted Puerto Rico’s political and economic development.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"In 1898, the United States conquered Puerto Rico as a result of the Spanish-American war.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"After the United States conquered Puerto Rico in 1898, Puerto Rico’s economy was transformed from a mix of small landowners and subsistence farmers into an agro-industrial economy dominated by U.S. companies.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"In the 1940s, U.S. policy promoted a manufacturing sector in Puerto Rico through Operation Bootstrap, but limited it to manufacturing industries that benefitted U.S. transnational corporations.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Operation Bootstrap in the 1940s was combined with the forced sterilization of many Puerto Rican women.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Puerto Rico was never allowed to define its own economic destiny by negotiating bilateral trade agreements.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Puerto Rico has had to adhere to fiscal policy directed by the United States.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"External control and extraction of profits stunted Puerto Rico’s productive base.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Recent changes in the U.S. tax code have caused the loss of thousands of manufacturing jobs and have been one of the factors leading to the current crisis.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

